Filed by langertha-adr-auditor during the k120-k127 drift audit (ADR 0010 symmetry check).

k124 (commit 2653715) taught ToolCall::from_anthropic to route tool_use input through
_decode_args, because the AKI.IO /anthropic shim ships input as a JSON *string* while real
Anthropic ships an object. After that fix four of the five inbound constructors decode a
stringified argument object; one does not:

  ToolCall.pm:77   from_openai     arguments => _decode_args( $fn->{arguments} )
  ToolCall.pm:94   from_anthropic  arguments => _decode_args( $block->{input} )      # k124
  ToolCall.pm:108  from_ollama     arguments => _decode_args( $fn->{arguments} )
  ToolCall.pm:143  from_responses  $args = _decode_args($args)
  ToolCall.pm:124  from_gemini     arguments => ( ref( $fc->{args} ) eq "HASH" ? $fc->{args} : {} )

So a Gemini-shaped functionCall whose args arrive as a JSON string is silently reduced to {}
-- the model called the tool, the tool runs with no arguments, and nothing warns. That is the
identical failure k124 was filed for.

Google native always sends args as an object, so this is not a live bug on the first-party
wire. It is a shim exposure: the same class of provider that produced k124 (a compatibility
endpoint re-encoding one dialect inside another -- OpenRouter, LM Studio, Vertex-style
proxies) is what would trip it, and Langertha ships several such engines.

Suggested fix (one line + a test, symmetric with k124):
  arguments => _decode_args( $fc->{args} ),
plus a case in t/91_tool_value_objects.t alongside the from_anthropic JSON-string case.

Consider at the same time whether _decode_args should be the documented single door for
every inbound argument blob, since ADR 0010 makes symmetry across the value objects the
stated property -- an asymmetry that has to be rediscovered per-constructor is the drift.

Verified at HEAD 07f6d68. Related: ADR 0001, ADR 0010, karr k124.
